message: "If you use this software or workflow in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Chemistry Lab Notebook for Obsidian"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Sakharov"
    given-names: "Pavel"
    affiliation: "Technion – Israel Institute of Technology"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Paivel/chemistry-lab-notebook-for-obsidian"
# For each release add version: "X.Y.Z" and date-released: "YYYY-MM-DD" here (the release workflow checks them).
abstract: >-
  A free and open-source electronic laboratory notebook workflow for synthetic
  chemistry, implemented as a reproducible Obsidian vault with reaction records,
  analytical-data integration, planning tools, templates, and local chemical
  structure and reaction searching.
keywords:
  - electronic laboratory notebook
  - ELN
  - chemistry
  - synthetic chemistry
  - Obsidian
  - reproducible research
  - chemical structure search
